    "detailed_description": "This game is a side-scrolling action game where you control Momotaro and fight against demons.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nYou can select a stage from the path in the base.<br />\r\nTry not to let your HP fall to zero while defeating enemies.<br />\r\nThere is a limit to the number of times you can use it, but you can recover it with millet dumplings.<br />\r\nMomotaro will become more powerful when you open the treasure chest in the stage.<br />\r\nWhen you reach the Jizo in the stage, you can recover and warp back and forth to the starting point.<br />\r\nDefeating the boss will clear the stage, and you will be able to add new friends and learn new techniques.<br />\r\nYou can call your friends by consuming a gauge.<br />\r\nYou can check your moves and return to your base on the menu screen.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nYou can use the keyboard or PS4 or XBOX360 controller to control the game.<br />\r\nSaving is done automatically.<br />\r\nJapanese and English languages are supported, and can be switched on the title screen.<br />\r\nPress F1 to go full screen.",
    "about_the_game": "This game is a side-scrolling action game where you control Momotaro and fight against demons.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nYou can select a stage from the path in the base.<br />\r\nTry not to let your HP fall to zero while defeating enemies.<br />\r\nThere is a limit to the number of times you can use it, but you can recover it with millet dumplings.<br />\r\nMomotaro will become more powerful when you open the treasure chest in the stage.<br />\r\nWhen you reach the Jizo in the stage, you can recover and warp back and forth to the starting point.<br />\r\nDefeating the boss will clear the stage, and you will be able to add new friends and learn new techniques.<br />\r\nYou can call your friends by consuming a gauge.<br />\r\nYou can check your moves and return to your base on the menu screen.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nYou can use the keyboard or PS4 or XBOX360 controller to control the game.<br />\r\nSaving is done automatically.<br />\r\nJapanese and English languages are supported, and can be switched on the title screen.<br />\r\nPress F1 to go full screen.",
